First, I need to ensure that the query retrieves data concerning the regular TV appearances, specifically related to voice performance types, and I need to identify the specific season (in this case, Season 1) since the pilot is part of that season. 

The logical form of the query will involve a JOIN operation that combines information about television shows, the roles of actors in those shows, and any specified conditions for seasons and character appearances. 

The steps I will take to formulate the S-expression query are as follows:
1. Identify the relationship connecting "tv", "regular tv appearance", and "actor".
2. Formulate conditions using JOIN to filter the appearances by season and performance type (voice).
3. Ensure that the character being queried is "Meg Griffin".

Putting this all together, the S-expression captures the relevant information to return the actor who voiced Meg in the pilot episode.
</think>

